The problem is on line 181. When searching stdin (no files), the code always uses `write_line_with_prefix("(standard input)", ...)` regardless of whether `-H` was provided. According to the spec, when there are no file operands and `-H` is NOT given, there should be NO prefix.

The fix: only use the prefix for stdin when `force_filename` (i.e., `-H`) is set.
